1
00:00:01,170 --> 00:00:08,220
In the year 850, the Colossal Titan
reappeared and demolished another wall.

2
00:00:08,430 --> 00:00:12,890
Once again, humanity allowed
the Titans to further their advance.

3
00:00:13,100 --> 00:00:17,060
One after another,
soldiers fell to the Titans.

4
00:00:17,270 --> 00:00:18,690
And then...

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:19,860
Eren!

6
00:00:20,060 --> 00:00:21,480
Hurry!

7
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:31,700
Eren fell prey to a Titan too.

8
00:00:32,540 --> 00:00:34,870
Man, Mikasa's incredible...

9
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:37,120
How can she move so fast?!

10
00:00:37,330 --> 00:00:40,210
No! She's not her usual,
composed self at all!

11
00:00:40,420 --> 00:00:42,290
I'll do whatever it takes to win!

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,760
Whatever it takes to live!

13
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:48,430
Mikasa found herself in
dire straits as well

14
00:00:48,630 --> 00:00:52,350
when a mysterious Titan
appeared and attacked another Titan.

15
00:01:15,410 --> 00:01:20,250
Unknown are the names
of the flowers that have been trampled

16
00:01:20,460 --> 00:01:25,710
Birds have fallen to the earth
and long for the wind

17
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:30,800
Prayers won't solve anything

18
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:36,140
Only the will to fight
can change the here and now!

19
00:01:36,350 --> 00:01:41,440
O pigs who laugh at the resolve
to walk over corpses to move forward

20
00:01:41,650 --> 00:01:43,980
Livestock complacency? False prosperity?

21
00:01:44,190 --> 00:01:46,860
Give us the freedom of dying,
starving wolves!

22
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:52,240
The humiliation of being caged
is what triggers us to fight back

23
00:01:52,450 --> 00:01:57,540
We hunters slaughter prey
beyond the castle walls,

24
00:01:57,750 --> 00:02:02,750
consumed with surging bloodlust,

25
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:09,880
as our crimson bows and arrows
pierce scarlet holes into the twilight

26
00:02:32,006 --> 00:02:37,011
I Can Hear His Heartbeat: The Struggle for Trost, Part 4

27
00:02:37,870 --> 00:02:38,660
There!

28
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:42,330
Your mobility gear still works,
and I've given you all my blades.

29
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:46,130
All I ask is that you
leave me with this one...

30
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:51,300
I'd rather not get
eaten alive, if I can help it.

31
00:02:57,220 --> 00:02:59,310
N-No way...

32
00:03:00,350 --> 00:03:01,770
Armin.

33
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:06,560
I'm not leaving you here.

34
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:13,070
B-But the place is swarming with Titans;

35
00:03:13,280 --> 00:03:15,280
you can't possibly
carry someone while jumping..

36
00:03:15,490 --> 00:03:16,910
Let's go!

37
00:03:18,580 --> 00:03:20,160
No...

38
00:03:20,370 --> 00:03:22,000
Please don't...

39
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,250
I'll only...

40
00:03:24,460 --> 00:03:27,670
I'll only get more of my friends killed!

41
00:03:38,930 --> 00:03:39,930
Wait!

42
00:03:40,140 --> 00:03:42,430
Listen! I have a suggestion!

43
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,270
A suggestion?

44
00:03:45,730 --> 00:03:50,570
Only you two can do it,
so I leave the choice to you...

45
00:03:50,770 --> 00:03:52,900
I know it sounds crazy,

46
00:03:53,110 --> 00:03:55,030
but could we use
that Titan to our advantage?

47
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:56,530
That Titan?!

48
00:03:56,740 --> 00:04:00,660
It attacks other Titans and
doesn't show any interest in us.

49
00:04:00,870 --> 00:04:05,540
So I'm wondering if we
could lead it to the supply building...

50
00:04:05,750 --> 00:04:10,670
If it takes out the other Titans
for us, we just might all survive!

51
00:04:10,880 --> 00:04:14,670
Lead it?! How do you
hope to lead that thing?!

52
00:04:14,880 --> 00:04:17,680
My guess is it's fighting on instinct.

53
00:04:17,890 --> 00:04:21,720
If you two take out the Titans around it,

54
00:04:21,930 --> 00:04:25,560
it'll go and look for other Titans.

55
00:04:25,770 --> 00:04:27,850
That'll naturally lead
it toward Headquarters.

56
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:31,440
W-We can't risk our
necks for some hopeful guess!

57
00:04:31,650 --> 00:04:34,490
But if it works, we could eliminate
all the Titans attacking HQ

58
00:04:34,690 --> 00:04:36,650
in one fell swoop!

59
00:04:38,410 --> 00:04:40,450
- It seems worth trying.
- Huh?!

60
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,030
Are you serious?!

61
00:04:42,240 --> 00:04:46,460
It's better to take a gamble than
wait for our inevitable deaths.

62
00:04:46,660 --> 00:04:49,040
Let's go with Armin's suggestion.

63
00:04:49,250 --> 00:04:52,040
You want us to
fight Titans with a Titan?!

64
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:54,250
Yes. I do.

65
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:59,890
If we fail, we'll be laughingstocks.

66
00:05:01,010 --> 00:05:04,180
But if we succeed, everyone survives.

67
00:05:04,390 --> 00:05:06,390
It all comes down to resolve.

68
00:05:08,230 --> 00:05:10,310
All right! Fine!

69
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,700
Am I really cut out for this?

70
00:05:19,950 --> 00:05:24,620
Am I really fit to have
a position of responsibility?

71
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:30,920
No!

72
00:05:31,130 --> 00:05:34,550
No... now is the time.

73
00:05:34,750 --> 00:05:39,170
Now is our chance, while the
Titans are preoccupied over there!

74
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:42,890
Now!

75
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:46,390
Make for HQ while we have the chance!

76
00:05:57,070 --> 00:05:58,360
Now is our only chance!

77
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:01,700
If we run out of gas,
it's all over anyway!

78
00:06:01,910 --> 00:06:03,740
Everyone, charge!

79
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:52,290
- Jean!
- Huh?

80
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:55,290
Thanks! You helped us get away!

81
00:06:55,500 --> 00:06:56,500
Huh?!

82
00:06:56,710 --> 00:06:57,750
It's all thanks to you!

83
00:06:57,960 --> 00:07:02,420
It's like I said before!
You make a good leader!

84
00:07:02,630 --> 00:07:05,340
I'm not so sure about that!

85
00:07:14,350 --> 00:07:15,770
Damn!

86
00:07:33,960 --> 00:07:36,250
How many made it?

87
00:07:38,960 --> 00:07:41,000
How many comrades' deaths did I use?!

88
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:45,430
How many people
died because of my orders?

89
00:07:54,890 --> 00:07:58,520
You're with the
supply team, aren't you?

90
00:07:58,730 --> 00:08:00,150
Yeah...

91
00:08:03,360 --> 00:08:04,360
Stop, Jean!

92
00:08:04,570 --> 00:08:07,490
These are the ones who abandoned us!

93
00:08:07,700 --> 00:08:10,410
People are dead because of you guys!

94
00:08:10,620 --> 00:08:13,250
The Titans overran the supply room!

95
00:08:13,450 --> 00:08:14,830
There was nothing we could do!

96
00:08:15,040 --> 00:08:18,380
It's your job to deal with it anyway!

97
00:08:21,380 --> 00:08:23,010
Hit the deck!

98
00:08:28,550 --> 00:08:29,760
Crap...!

99
00:08:30,260 --> 00:08:33,180
There are too many people!

100
00:08:33,390 --> 00:08:34,560
- Hurry!
- Get further inside!

101
00:08:34,770 --> 00:08:36,440
Stop! We can't all go at once!

102
00:08:36,640 --> 00:08:38,020
Where'd Mikasa go?!

103
00:08:38,230 --> 00:08:41,690
She ran out of gas!
She's long gone by now!

104
00:08:42,020 --> 00:08:43,650
This is normal...

105
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:46,990
This must be what the real world is like...

106
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:51,700
Was I trying to
delude myself up until now?

107
00:08:51,910 --> 00:08:56,830
Surely I knew what
the real world was like...

108
00:08:57,040 --> 00:09:00,880
It's so obvious when you think about it...

109
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:06,470
There's no way we stand a
chance against these monstrosities...

110
00:09:15,310 --> 00:09:16,730
What?!

111
00:09:27,490 --> 00:09:28,820
Huh?

112
00:09:29,030 --> 00:09:30,950
What the hell...?

113
00:09:35,080 --> 00:09:35,950
Mikasa!

114
00:09:36,160 --> 00:09:39,210
Man, that was close.
It's completely empty.

115
00:09:39,410 --> 00:09:42,630
We did it! We managed to make it!

116
00:09:42,830 --> 00:09:45,880
Wh-Whoa, you're alive!

117
00:09:46,090 --> 00:09:47,420
- We did it, Armin!
- O-Ouch!

118
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:50,260
Your plan worked!

119
00:09:50,470 --> 00:09:51,260
Guys!

120
00:09:51,470 --> 00:09:54,430
That Titan's an Abnormal!
It's killin' all the other Titans!

121
00:09:54,640 --> 00:09:57,770
And it has no interest in us!

122
00:09:57,980 --> 00:10:01,810
We can use it to our
advantage to escape from here!

123
00:10:02,810 --> 00:10:04,900
Use a Titan?!

124
00:10:05,110 --> 00:10:07,480
A Titan, helping us?!

125
00:10:07,690 --> 00:10:11,150
- What kind of nonsensical dream...
- It's no dream.

126
00:10:11,360 --> 00:10:13,700
Whether it's an Abnormal
or not, I don't care.

127
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:18,200
We're going to let it rampage
here for as long as possible.

128
00:10:22,250 --> 00:10:28,920
Because, realistically, that's our
best strategy for survival now.

129
00:10:50,400 --> 00:10:51,820
It's okay.

130
00:10:52,030 --> 00:10:55,320
That Titan's tougher than ordinary ones.

131
00:10:58,700 --> 00:11:01,540
I doubt they'll take down this building

132
00:11:01,750 --> 00:11:05,830
while that one's rampaging like crazy.

133
00:11:06,040 --> 00:11:10,260
How much do you know about that Titan?

134
00:11:11,340 --> 00:11:14,340
We can worry about that after we're safe.

135
00:11:14,550 --> 00:11:17,720
Yeah. Let's survive first.

136
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:19,470
We found some!

137
00:11:19,680 --> 00:11:22,100
They belong to the Military Police!

138
00:11:22,310 --> 00:11:25,100
Damn things are all covered in dust...

139
00:11:26,270 --> 00:11:29,440
Are you sure buckshot
is what we want to use?!

140
00:11:29,650 --> 00:11:32,150
I mean, seriously...

141
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:36,450
Will guns even work against Titans?

142
00:11:38,120 --> 00:11:40,830
They're far better than nothing, I feel.

143
00:11:41,040 --> 00:11:44,960
If there are still seven Titans in the supply
room that are three or four meters tall,

144
00:11:45,170 --> 00:11:50,210
this much firepower should be capable
of blinding them all simultaneously.

145
00:11:50,420 --> 00:11:54,840
First, we'll use the lift to lower a
group of people from the center ceiling.

146
00:11:55,050 --> 00:11:59,390
They'll then simultaneously fire
at the faces of each of the seven Titans,

147
00:11:59,600 --> 00:12:01,180
thereby blinding them.

148
00:12:01,390 --> 00:12:06,190
Then comes the moment of truth...

149
00:12:06,400 --> 00:12:08,150
Seven people hiding up top

150
00:12:08,360 --> 00:12:12,440
will strike the Titans'
vitals just after the guns fire.

151
00:12:12,650 --> 00:12:17,530
In other words, this plan
will put everything on the line...

152
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,660
everyone's lives on the line...

153
00:12:19,870 --> 00:12:21,490
for a single attack.

154
00:12:22,620 --> 00:12:27,960
Seven people will have to slay seven
Titans at the same time in a single blow.

155
00:12:28,750 --> 00:12:34,460
It'll be up to the seven most physically
fit and adept soldiers we have here.

156
00:12:34,670 --> 00:12:40,260
So, umm, I'm sorry for placing
everyone's lives on your shoulders...

157
00:12:40,470 --> 00:12:41,720
It's no problem.

158
00:12:41,930 --> 00:12:46,060
If we fail, we die. The risk's
the same regardless of who goes.

159
00:12:46,270 --> 00:12:52,940
Still, is this shabby idea of
mine really our best strategy?

160
00:12:53,150 --> 00:12:58,700
We got no other choice.
We're out of time and options.

161
00:12:58,910 --> 00:13:00,870
All we can do now is give it our all!

162
00:13:01,070 --> 00:13:04,620
It'll be fine. Be confident.

163
00:13:04,830 --> 00:13:07,160
You have a knack for
figuring out correct solutions.

164
00:13:07,370 --> 00:13:08,210
Huh?

165
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:12,210
You even used it to save
my life and Eren's life before.

166
00:13:12,420 --> 00:13:16,050
It did...? When?

167
00:13:17,260 --> 00:13:18,970
The lift's ready!

168
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:21,800
The guns too! They're all loaded!

169
00:13:22,010 --> 00:13:23,720
You just don't realize it.

170
00:13:23,930 --> 00:13:26,100
- We can talk about it later.
- Yeah.

171
00:13:28,520 --> 00:13:33,730
Still, can we really take out all
the Titans without our ODM gear?

172
00:13:33,940 --> 00:13:35,070
Of course we can!

173
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:37,320
These Titans are only three or four meters tall.

174
00:13:37,530 --> 00:13:39,570
Targeting their vitals will be a cinch.

175
00:13:39,780 --> 00:13:40,660
Yeah.

176
00:13:40,860 --> 00:13:44,700
Regardless of size, their vitals go
from the head to the nape of the neck...

177
00:13:44,910 --> 00:13:47,700
...one meter high and ten centimeters across!

178
00:13:47,910 --> 00:13:50,830
You can also shove
one of these up their asses!

179
00:13:51,040 --> 00:13:52,920
Those are their only two weak spots!

180
00:13:53,130 --> 00:13:55,710
I never knew about that one!

181
00:13:55,920 --> 00:13:58,510
This is the first I've heard of it, too.

182
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,010
Reiner.

183
00:14:00,220 --> 00:14:03,930
Those could end up
being your last words, you know.

184
00:14:17,190 --> 00:14:20,110
Good. Their numbers haven't increased.

185
00:14:25,580 --> 00:14:28,120
Proceeding with operation!

186
00:14:37,210 --> 00:14:40,670
Stay clam! We need
to lure them all the way in!

187
00:14:45,010 --> 00:14:46,430
Steady...

188
00:14:48,930 --> 00:14:51,560
Avoid a disadvantageous fight...

189
00:14:51,770 --> 00:14:54,270
If you don't want anyone to die...

190
00:14:54,480 --> 00:14:57,360
...then make this attack count!

191
00:14:58,280 --> 00:15:00,110
Steady...

192
00:15:07,660 --> 00:15:09,080
Ready...

193
00:15:14,830 --> 00:15:16,250
Fire!

194
00:15:25,430 --> 00:15:26,220
I got mine!

195
00:15:26,430 --> 00:15:28,560
How about you guys?!

196
00:15:37,020 --> 00:15:38,610
U-Umm...

197
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:41,650
- I'm sorry for suddenly sneaking up and...
- C-Crap...

198
00:15:41,860 --> 00:15:44,360
I'm very sorry...!

199
00:15:44,570 --> 00:15:45,740
Sasha and Conny!

200
00:15:45,950 --> 00:15:48,070
Hurry! Lend them backup!

201
00:15:49,740 --> 00:15:53,500
I'm... umm...

202
00:15:53,710 --> 00:15:55,710
I'm very sorry!

203
00:16:07,470 --> 00:16:09,640
Mikasa!

204
00:16:09,850 --> 00:16:11,970
You saved me!

205
00:16:12,180 --> 00:16:13,100
Are you all right?

206
00:16:13,310 --> 00:16:14,230
Thanks to you!

207
00:16:14,430 --> 00:16:15,810
Then get up.

208
00:16:16,020 --> 00:16:17,400
I owe you one...

209
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:18,440
No problem.

210
00:16:18,650 --> 00:16:20,400
Oh, man.

211
00:16:20,610 --> 00:16:22,530
That was a close call, Annie.

212
00:16:22,730 --> 00:16:25,280
I'm really glad you didn't end up hurt.

213
00:16:25,490 --> 00:16:27,410
They've all been slain!

214
00:16:27,610 --> 00:16:28,990
Switch to resupply work!

215
00:16:29,200 --> 00:16:31,030
We did it!

216
00:16:36,410 --> 00:16:40,000
- All right! We're gonna survive!
- And no more Titans are coming inside!

217
00:16:40,210 --> 00:16:43,340
All thanks to that
berserk Titan out there!

218
00:16:44,760 --> 00:16:47,430
I caved in to that Titan...

219
00:16:47,630 --> 00:16:49,550
I'm too ashamed to face the others...!

220
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:51,550
There'll be plenty of
time to sneer at you later!

221
00:16:51,760 --> 00:16:53,350
For now, we gotta escape!

222
00:16:54,390 --> 00:16:57,770
I can't see myself as much of a leader.

223
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:00,270
Don't talk like that anymore.

224
00:17:04,230 --> 00:17:06,990
I don't mean any offense by this,

225
00:17:07,200 --> 00:17:09,990
but I think the fact you aren't strong

226
00:17:10,200 --> 00:17:12,830
really lets you understand
how the weak feel.

227
00:17:13,030 --> 00:17:17,330
And your skill at recognizing
a situation as it unfolds

228
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:21,500
gives you a clear grasp of what
needs to be done now, you know?

229
00:17:22,540 --> 00:17:24,800
You made the right call.

230
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,840
It's what got me moving.
It's why I'm alive now.

231
00:17:34,600 --> 00:17:37,020
Everyone ready?! It's time to scram!

232
00:17:37,230 --> 00:17:40,060
- Let's move!
- Scale the wall!

233
00:17:40,270 --> 00:17:42,270
Rendezvous with the main forces!

234
00:17:44,150 --> 00:17:45,570
Mikasa?!

235
00:17:49,700 --> 00:17:50,780
Mikasa!

236
00:17:50,990 --> 00:17:52,740
We have to get out of here!

237
00:17:52,950 --> 00:17:54,660
That Titan...

238
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:00,500
They're cannibalizing it?!

239
00:18:02,960 --> 00:18:05,710
I guess it can't regenerate its body?

240
00:18:06,840 --> 00:18:10,430
I thought that if we could somehow
figure out what's up with that Titan,

241
00:18:10,630 --> 00:18:15,850
it could've helped us break
free from this hopeless situation...

242
00:18:16,060 --> 00:18:17,770
I agree.

243
00:18:17,970 --> 00:18:21,640
We'll learn nothing at all
if it ends up getting eaten!

244
00:18:21,850 --> 00:18:25,770
For now, we have to get
rid of the ones clinging to it

245
00:18:25,980 --> 00:18:27,360
and help keep it alive!

246
00:18:27,570 --> 00:18:28,780
Are you insane, Reiner?!

247
00:18:28,990 --> 00:18:31,610
We can finally get our asses out of here!

248
00:18:31,820 --> 00:18:36,950
And what if there's a chance
that Titan could become our ally?

249
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:40,040
It'd be a more powerful weapon
than any cannon, wouldn't you agree?

250
00:18:41,160 --> 00:18:42,620
Ally...?

251
00:18:42,830 --> 00:18:44,670
Are you actually serious?!

252
00:18:46,130 --> 00:18:47,590
That one...!

253
00:18:48,250 --> 00:18:51,670
That's the Abnormal that ate Thomas!

254
00:19:25,250 --> 00:19:26,670
Oh, man...

255
00:19:31,670 --> 00:19:34,510
What was it you wanted to save again?

256
00:19:41,220 --> 00:19:44,980
Looks like it's finished for good.

257
00:19:45,190 --> 00:19:47,520
All right, that's enough! Let's get going!

258
00:19:47,730 --> 00:19:50,360
As if that monster would ever be our ally...

259
00:19:50,570 --> 00:19:52,610
A Titan's a Titan.

260
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:59,200
What's with you guys?

261
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:24,520
Mikasa!

262
00:21:33,840 --> 00:21:35,670
It's Eren...

263
00:21:36,920 --> 00:21:42,640
His severed arm and leg are back...

264
00:21:42,850 --> 00:21:47,850
He'd been swallowed by a Titan back then...

265
00:21:48,060 --> 00:21:49,480
Back then...

266
00:21:58,530 --> 00:22:02,070
How is this possible?

267
00:22:09,750 --> 00:22:16,880
Does this mean Eren did all this...?

268
00:22:36,520 --> 00:22:41,450
Your dreams are where your heart is

269
00:22:41,650 --> 00:22:47,700
They're more fragile than life itself

270
00:22:47,910 --> 00:22:52,370
Over and over you cast them aside,
only to find more

271
00:22:52,580 --> 00:22:59,050
Now, rest in peace

272
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:10,390
Pounding impulses defile the things we wish for

273
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:20,650
and the more we forget
the more we remember again

274
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:26,620
In this beautiful, cruel world

275
00:23:26,820 --> 00:23:31,790
all I can do is ask why we're still alive

276
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:37,500
Oh, with our strength... and our weakness...

277
00:23:37,710 --> 00:23:43,170
what are we going to protect if there's no sense

278
00:23:43,380 --> 00:23:46,800
to anything anymore?

279
00:23:53,140 --> 00:23:55,350
"I'm going to drive out the Titans."

280
00:23:55,560 --> 00:23:59,940
That strong emotion
transformed Eren into a Titan.

281
00:24:00,150 --> 00:24:04,650
However, the Garrison Regiment
deems him a threat to humanity

282
00:24:04,860 --> 00:24:04,964
and turns its swords at him.

283
00:24:04,964 --> 00:24:07,008
Whereabouts of His Left Arm: The Struggle for Trost, Part 5
and turns its swords at him.

284
00:24:07,008 --> 00:24:07,030
and turns its swords at him.
